  "Comments": "Phospholipids of crude soybean oil (lecithin), lumped as one liquid lipid: the dilinoleoyl species of PC, PE, PI and PA mixed as soybean lecithin (AOCS Lipid Library, Dijkstra, Table 1: 32, 23, 21 and 8 wt %), one P atom per molecule, so 1 ppm of P is 25.13 ppm of phosphatides (AOCS: about 25). Nonvolatile (the squalene vapor pressure divided by 1e6). Critical constants set for a heavy lipid. Liquid density 1030 kg/m3 at 20 C (to be checked); heat capacity of soybean oil per unit mass (Garcia Rojas 2013). Formation enthalpy and the other properties of squalene per unit mass: the phosphatides don't react in the refining blocks, so only their heat capacity enters the energy balances.",
